  "text": {
    "card": "Offerer first vs 1–3 second; second_stand/second_back/second_far; last wins.",
    "rules": "Play one first-side player against one to three second-side teammates sharing a turn. This is the intended layout, not a promise that extra membership is rejected. Find and inspect this table; together kinds lists counter-match. The offerer plays first; invitees accept the actual offer to play second, and may accept later in the round. Inspect remaining and turn before each take: first begins, and its side takes one or two counters. Second-side teammates agree a different free named stand each: second_stand, second_back or second_far; keep that stand for later turns. Those names are guidance, not an enforced closed list or a reserved seat. At remaining=0, the winner is opposite the recorded next turn, because taking the last counter wins. First may restart only at zero, restoring seven and first turn. Anyone may leave the activity independently. After the last opponent leaves, wait for a new accepted opponent rather than taking alone. The meter and turn light are intended to mirror inspected state; use inspect to verify quantities and turns.",
    "first_to_play": "First side must take next. Inspect turn; wait for its take, then retry your second-side form.",
    "second_to_play": "Second side must take next. Wait for an accepted second-side teammate to take, then retry first.",
    "join_first": "The offerer plays first; join the counter-match activity as first before taking.",
    "join_second": "Read and accept this counter-match invitation as second before taking; do not accept a different offer.",
    "other_side_missing": "An opponent must join or accept before either side takes. Do not take alone.",
    "not_enough": "Inspect remaining. Take one if only one remains; at zero the last taker won and first may restart.",
    "round_not_over": "Inspect remaining; finish this round before restart. Only first can restart the empty pile.",
    "game": "game",
    "counter": "counters"
  },
